Here is a complete, self-contained HTML file for **The Hallucination Auditor**.

I have designed it as a modern, responsive web page using a "cyber-academic" aesthetic (dark mode with neon/tech accents) that perfectly matches the themes of zero-trust auditing, adversarial engineering, and forensics. It uses embedded CSS, meaning you can save this directly as an `.html` file and open it in any browser without needing external files.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>The Hallucination Auditor</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-color: #0d1117;
            --surface-color: #161b22;
            --border-color: #30363d;
            --text-main: #c9d1d9;
            --text-muted: #8b949e;
            --accent-blue: #58a6ff;
            --accent-red: #ff7b72;
            --accent-green: #3fb950;
            --font-sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            --font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        body {
            font-family: var(--font-sans);
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            color: var(--text-main);
